
# Cursor Rules

## Main Purpose

- **Primary Goal**: This website (halatto.app) is a landing page and how-to guide site for the iOS app Vintage Photo Filter – Halatto, an iPhone photo editor that makes existing photos look shot on film or an old camera (35mm, disposable, instant, toy camera, Y2K digicam) with grain, aging, light leaks, flash and a date stamp (https://apps.apple.com/app/id6758913511). Facts about the app and the keyword research live in `app.md`. All content, design, and functionality should be optimized to promote and drive downloads of the iOS app. There is deliberately no online editor on the site: the site answers iPhone-specific questions and sends readers to the app.

## File Modification Rules

- **DO NOT** modify `index.html` - it is a generated file. All HTML changes should be made in `build/template.html` instead.
- When making changes to the template, update `build/template.html` and regenerate the HTML files using the build script.

## Project Structure

- `build/template.html` - Main template file for generating HTML
- `build/build.js` - Build script that generates HTML from template
- `build/*.json` - Page copy per language (`en.json` is the source; add a locale by creating `build/<code>.json` and listing it in `LANGUAGES` in `build/constants.js`)
- `build/constants.js` - Site URL, App Store id, languages, guide config, IndexNow key
- `build/partials/*.html` - Shared head, header, footer, App Store button, final CTA, analytics
- `build/guides/*.json` - SEO guide pages (one JSON per target keyword, see the keyword table in `app.md`) rendered with `build/guide-template.html`; the hub uses `build/guides-hub-template.html`
- `index.html`, `guides/**/index.html` - Generated files (do not edit directly)
- `*/index.html` - Generated files for language-specific pages - do not edit directly
- `llms.txt`, `urls.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, `robots.txt` - Generated by `npm run build` / `npm run sitemap`
- `img/` - App icon, favicons, QR code and App Store screenshots (`img/screenshots/N.webp` 460×995 and `N@2x.webp`, downloaded from the App Store listing; replace by hand when the listing changes). `img/looks/*.svg` are the 14 camera icons; `img/brand/` holds the hero camera and print art; `img/appstore/` keeps the 1024 px icon and a contact sheet of the screenshots.
- `style.css` - Main stylesheet
- `site.js` - Mobile menu, screenshot strip keyboard scroll, FAQ collapse on small screens
- `privacy.html` - Privacy policy page
- `terms.html` - Terms of service page
- `package.json` - Node.js dependencies and scripts
- `fonts/` - Self-hosted Michroma (display) as a Latin woff subset plus the full ttf fallback; `@font-face` lives at the top of `style.css`. Body text uses the system font stack. No Google Fonts requests.

## Design rules

- Palette ("darkroom at golden hour", same as the app's Constants.AppColors): ink #17120F, charcoal #221B17, umber #2E2520, cream #F4EAD8, sun #FFD36B, mustard #F7B733, amber #E89A1F, toffee #C97A12, coral #F08A5D, date orange #FF8A1E.
- Michroma only for headings, eyebrows and short labels; body text in the system font.
- Golden gradient sections (hero, final CTA) frame the dark page; everything else sits on ink/charcoal cards with 1px cream hairlines.
- The hero camera ejecting a developing print is the one loud element; keep other sections quiet. Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
- Screenshots sit on a film strip with sprocket holes.

## Copy rules

- Never claim affiliation with Apple, Kodak, Fujifilm, Polaroid, Olympus or CineStill; use brand names only descriptively ("Polaroid-style").
- Do not invent UI labels: use the labels listed in `app.md` (Looks, Aging, Light Leak, Flash, Date stamp, Develop the Roll, Save as Recipe, Export / Share video).
- Pricing: free to try with a daily limit; subscription or lifetime purchase removes it. No ratings in JSON-LD until the listing has enough.
